======================================================================
  R-VALUE VERIFICATION FROM RAW DATA
======================================================================

Q1: Do numeric 1-5 attractor scores exist?
   ANSWER: NO.
   All crawler results contain ONLY categorical labels:
   - trajectory: 'stable' | 'deteriorating' | 'improving'
   - confidence: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low'
   No numeric 1-5 scores were ever produced.

Q2: Verifying r=0.564 (SP500 crawler) and r=0.316 (baseline)
------------------------------------------------------------
   Matched winner/trap cases: 103
   Encoding: improving=1.5, stable=1, deteriorating=0
   Outcome: winner=1, trap=-1
   Correlation method: Spearman rank

   REPORTED r=0.316 (baseline)   → COMPUTED r=0.3156 (n=103, p=0.000830)
   REPORTED r=0.564 (enriched)   → COMPUTED r=0.5644 (n=103, p=0.000000)

   Alt encoding (stable+improving=1, deteriorating=0):
   Baseline: r=0.3156, Enriched: r=0.5653

Q3: Verifying r=0.410 (mid-cap baseline v2) and r=0.455 (enriched v2)
------------------------------------------------------------
   Matched winner/trap cases: 80
   REPORTED r=0.410 (baseline v2) → COMPUTED r=0.4100 (n=80, p=0.000072)
